            <ArticleTitle>Silent myocardial infarction during hypoglycaemic coma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of silent myocardial infarction associated with hypoglycaemic coma is described. A hypoglycaemic episode represents a risk factor for a patient with underlying ischaemic heart disease. A routine ECG may be indicated in such circumstances.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
